{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the kohen who is anointed, etc.</b> This atonement of Yom HaKippurim is valid only with a Kohen Gadol (Yoma 73); since the entire passage is spoken of Aaron, it was necessary to say of the Kohen Gadol who comes after him that he is like him." "<b>And who fills his hand.</b> I have only the one anointed with the anointing oil — the one invested with many garments, from where? Scripture says: ״וַאֲשֶׁר יְמַלֵּא אֶת יָדוֹ״ and so forth; and they are all the Kohanim Gedolim who served from Yoshiyahu onward, for in his days the flask of anointing oil was hidden away (Horayot 12)." "<b>In place of his father.</b> To teach that if his son fills his place, he takes precedence over anyone (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:50.164522199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}